{
  "an10.91:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 10.91 ",
  "an10.91:0.2": "10. With Upāli ",
  "an10.91:0.3": "Pleasure Seekers ",
  "an10.91:1.1": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery. ",
  "an10.91:1.2": "Then the householder Anāthapiṇḍika went up to the Buddha, bowed, and sat down to one side. Seated to one side, the Buddha said to the householder Anāthapiṇḍika: ",
  "an10.91:2.1": "“These ten pleasure seekers are found in the world. ",
  "an10.91:2.2": "What ten? ",
  "an10.91:2.3": "First, a pleasure seeker seeks wealth using illegitimate, coercive means. ",
  "an10.91:2.4": "They don’t make themselves happy and pleased, nor share it and make merit. ",
  "an10.91:3.1": "Next, a pleasure seeker seeks wealth using illegitimate, coercive means. ",
  "an10.91:3.2": "They make themselves happy and pleased, but don’t share it and make merit. ",
  "an10.91:4.1": "Next, a pleasure seeker seeks wealth using illegitimate, coercive means. ",
  "an10.91:4.2": "They make themselves happy and pleased, and they share it and make merit. ",
  "an10.91:5.1": "Next, a pleasure seeker seeks wealth using means both legitimate and illegitimate, and coercive and non-coercive. ",
  "an10.91:5.2": "They don’t make themselves happy and pleased, nor share it and make merit. ",
  "an10.91:6.1": "Next, a pleasure seeker seeks wealth using means both legitimate and illegitimate, and coercive and non-coercive. ",
  "an10.91:6.2": "They make themselves happy an